Pretty much—though we’re not merely ingredients. We’re vortices that learned to notice the soup.

Earth spins, circles the Sun, the Sun crosses the galaxy, and the galaxy moves through expanding spacetime. Inside us, matter and energy continually enter, reorganize, and leave. What persists is less the original material than the pattern coordinating its passage.

\text{self} \approx \text{stable pattern within continuous flow}

Whirlpools with names. Cosmic soup briefly organized enough to love, argue, build pyramids, invent gods, and wonder what the hell soup is.